<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<ui version="4.0">
 <class>AnalyzeEEGComplexityDoc</class>
 <widget class="QWidget" name="AnalyzeEEGComplexityDoc">
  <property name="geometry">
   <rect>
    <x>0</x>
    <y>0</y>
    <width>730</width>
    <height>590</height>
   </rect>
  </property>
  <property name="windowTitle">
   <string/>
  </property>
  <property name="styleSheet">
   <string notr="true">font: 12pt &quot;Roboto&quot;;</string>
  </property>
  <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="verticalLayout">
   <property name="spacing">
    <number>25</number>
   </property>
   <item>
    <widget class="QLabel" name="label">
     <property name="enabled">
      <bool>true</bool>
     </property>
     <property name="font">
      <font>
       <family>Roboto</family>
       <pointsize>12</pointsize>
       <italic>false</italic>
       <bold>false</bold>
      </font>
     </property>
     <property name="text">
      <string>&lt;html&gt;&lt;head/&gt;&lt;body&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Analyze EEG Complexity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
   <item>
    <widget class="QTextEdit" name="textEdit">
     <property name="html">
      <string>&lt;!DOCTYPE HTML PUBLIC &quot;-//W3C//DTD HTML 4.0//EN&quot; &quot;http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40/strict.dtd&quot;&gt;
&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;&lt;meta name=&quot;qrichtext&quot; content=&quot;1&quot; /&gt;&lt;meta charset=&quot;utf-8&quot; /&gt;&lt;style type=&quot;text/css&quot;&gt;
p, li { white-space: pre-wrap; }
hr { height: 1px; border-width: 0; }
li.unchecked::marker { content: &quot;\2610&quot;; }
li.checked::marker { content: &quot;\2612&quot;; }
&lt;/style&gt;&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body style=&quot; font-family:'Roboto'; font-size:12pt; font-weight:400; font-style:normal;&quot;&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Joint Lempel–Ziv complexity (joint)&lt;/span&gt; quantifies the compressibility of multichannel EEG by treating all selected channels together at each time point (Zozor et al., 2005). Lower values indicate more stereotyped/compressible dynamics; values near 1 after surrogate normalization indicate little structure beyond the power spectrum.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Concatenated Lempel–Ziv complexity (concat)&lt;/span&gt; first concatenates channels into a single binary sequence (Schartner et al., 2015), then computes Lempel–Ziv complexity on that longer string.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; font-weight:700;&quot;&gt;Univariate Lempel–Ziv complexity (univariate)&lt;/span&gt; computes a normalized complexity for each channel and summarizes across channels (median per epoch), following the approach used by Toker et al. (2022). This mode is recommended for high-density EEG montages.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;This tool computes Fourier-surrogate–normalized Lempel–Ziv complexity (FJZC) as described by Toker et al. (2022), based on Lempel–Ziv complexity (Lempel &amp;amp; Ziv, 1976; Kaspar &amp;amp; Schuster, 1987), joint multivariate LZC (Zozor et al., 2005), and concatenated multivariate LZC (Schartner et al., 2015). Signals are binarized from the Hilbert amplitude envelope and normalized against phase-randomized Fourier transform (FT) surrogates (Lancaster et al., 2018).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Important note:&lt;br /&gt;Joint mode with a large number of channels (high-density EEG) can produce normalized values close to 1 because the joint state space becomes very large relative to the epoch length. For dense montages, prefer univariate. Concat mode is computationally intensive on high-density data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;1 - Input Files:&lt;br /&gt;Add your PSG files (.edf, .sts or .eeg).&lt;br /&gt;The .tsv file is also needed for the edf format.&lt;br /&gt;The .sig file is also needed for the Stellate format.&lt;br /&gt;The whole NATUS subject folder is also needed for the NATUS format.&lt;br /&gt;Select the montage and the EEG channels to include in the analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;2 - Events Exclusion:&lt;br /&gt;Select events to discard from the analysis (i.e. artefacts previously detected and saved in the accessory file).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Important note:&lt;br /&gt;Complexity analysis should be performed on brain EEG channels. Any channels marked with the annotation group &amp;quot;art_inspector&amp;quot; and the name &amp;quot;art_channel&amp;quot; or &amp;quot;non_brain&amp;quot; will be automatically excluded from the analysis when that exclusion is configured in the process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;3 - Annotation Selection:&lt;br /&gt;Choose the recording scope for the analysis:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul style=&quot;margin-top: 0px; margin-bottom: 0px; margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px; -qt-list-indent: 1;&quot;&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Sleep Stages to analyze specific stages&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:0px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Unscored to analyze the full recording or a chosen time segment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot; margin-top:0px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;Specific Annotations to base the analysis on event markers&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;If the analysis is performed on specific annotations, select them in this step.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;4 - Complexity Settings:&lt;br /&gt;Define the complexity mode (joint, concat, or univariate; default: joint).&lt;br /&gt;Specify the epoch length and epoch overlap (in seconds).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;note:&lt;br /&gt;Epochs that contain rejected artefacts (NaN/Inf) or are entirely flat/zero are excluded before complexity is computed.&lt;br /&gt;Concat mode can be substantially slower than joint or univariate on high-density EEG.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;References:&lt;br /&gt;[1] Lempel, A., &amp;amp; Ziv, J. (1976). On the complexity of finite sequences. IEEE Transactions on Information Theory, 22(1), 75–81. &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1976.1055501&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#003e92;&quot;&gt;https://doi.org/10.1109/TIT.1976.1055501&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;[2] Kaspar, F., &amp;amp; Schuster, H. G. (1987). Easily calculable measure for the complexity of spatiotemporal patterns. Physical Review A, 36(2), 842–848. &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.36.842&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#003e92;&quot;&gt;https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevA.36.842&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;[3] Zozor, S., Ravier, P., &amp;amp; Buttelli, O. (2005). On Lempel–Ziv complexity for multidimensional data analysis. Physica A, 345(1–2), 285–302. &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physa.2004.07.024&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#003e92;&quot;&gt;https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physa.2004.07.024&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;[4] Schartner, M., Seth, A., Noirhomme, Q., Boly, M., Bruno, M.-A., Laureys, S., &amp;amp; Barrett, A. (2015). Complexity of multi-dimensional spontaneous EEG decreases during propofol-induced general anaesthesia. PLoS ONE, 10(8), e0133532. &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0133532&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#003e92;&quot;&gt;https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0133532&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;[5] Toker, D., Pappas, I., Lendner, J. D., Frohlich, J., Mateos, D. M., Mofakham, S., … &amp;amp; Monti, M. M. (2022). Consciousness is supported by near-critical slow cortical electrodynamics. Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences, 119(7), e2024455119. &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2024455119&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#003e92;&quot;&gt;https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.2024455119&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot; margin-top:12px; margin-bottom:12px; margin-left:0px; margin-right:0px; -qt-block-indent:0; text-indent:0px;&quot;&gt;[6] Lancaster, G., Iatsenko, D., Pidde, A., Ticcinelli, V., &amp;amp; Stefanovska, A. (2018). Surrogate data for hypothesis testing of physical systems. Physics Reports, 748, 1–60. &lt;a href=&quot;https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physrep.2018.06.001&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot; text-decoration: underline; color:#003e92;&quot;&gt;https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physrep.2018.06.001&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;</string>
     </property>
    </widget>
   </item>
  </layout>
 </widget>
